<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Račí údolí and Čertovy kazatelny circuit — Javorník, Račí údolí, Čertovy kazatelny and castle courtyard circuit [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>Walk from the Javorník railway platform through town, follow the blue-marked Račí valley approach past Tančírna, and take the full green serpentine to the main railed Čertovy kazatelny viewpoint. Return from that viewpoint spur and continue through St Antonín and the Jánský Vrch outdoor park, courtyard and view terrace to town and the same station walking ground. The complete circuit is approximately 8.7 km. Blue, green and red marked legs require attention at urban and station junctions; continuous signs are not claimed on every terminal edge.

The full circuit requires Jánský Vrch courtyard access during actual castle opening hours. Check current owner hours and on-site restrictions; if the required courtyard is closed, the complete itinerary is unavailable. Do not shorten or bypass it. Courtyard entry is free without a guide or interior ticket; park paths are free.

Stay on established walking paths and the full green serpentine and railed main viewpoint approach; avoid eroding shortcuts, fragile slopes and off-path park access.

Dogs must be leashed and waste removed; children under 15 require an accompanying adult in the castle grounds. Temporary operational or safety closures may apply.

Steep woodland slopes, steps, wet rock, leaves and winter ice require care. Plan daylight walking and check current path conditions.

Inherited 407 m ascent, 407 m descent and 210 minutes are approximate planning values; no measured elevation profile is supplied.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL1.0 — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright; https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/. Complete source ways, nodes and walking parents supply331 literal positions/330 directed source edges,53 source intervals. Only identical shared junction positions are removed. Canonical display uses the existing source-vertex helper; default variant and private planning GPX preserve all literal edges. No private GPS, guide-map, protected-polygon or raster coordinates, snaps, synthetic connectors or elevations. Two-dimensional planning geometry; not navigation-grade or legal permission.

